#: ../../source/generated/modules/freeports_dev.ci.render.rst:2
msgid "freeports\\_dev.ci.render"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.render:1 of
msgid ""
"``freeports-dev ci-report``: what a gate run looks like once it is "
"written down."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.render:3 of
msgid ""
"The measurement commands establish facts and write them into "
"``reports/``; :mod:`freeports_dev.ci.gate` judges them; this renders the "
"judgement, and does nothing else. That is the same three-way split "
"``freeports-validate`` follows — ``collect``, ``report``, ``check-"
"grants`` — and it is here for the same reason: a rendering that measured "
"something of its own would be a second source of truth for a figure the "
"gate already decided about."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.render:9 of
msgid ""
"Every rendering is a pure function of the model, which is why the model "
"exists at all::"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.render:17 of
msgid ""
"The first of those answers questions no rendering here anticipated, and "
"it stays available however the others change."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.render:20 of
msgid ""
"**This command never refuses anything.** ``ci-check`` decides whether a "
"commit is made; this says what the run found, and exits non-zero only "
"when it could not write what it was asked to write. A hook that could be "
"stopped by its own report would be a hook people remove."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.render:24 of
msgid ""
"**Nothing here carries a timestamp, and no rendering names a commit "
"unless a figure is stale.** These artefacts are committed — badges in a "
"``README.md``, tables in a documentation tree — and a date, or the head "
"recorded beside every figure, would put a diff in every commit saying "
"nothing had changed. The commit is named in exactly the place where it is"
" the news: beside a figure that was measured at another one."
msgstr ""

